  "lead": "State government tax collections were <b>$393.07 billion</b> in the first quarter of 2026, +5.7% from a year earlier, excluding D.C. (SRC-629-01). Massachusetts collected <b>$11.62 billion</b>, rank 8 of 50 (derived, SRC-629-01). State governments employed <b>4,441,091</b> full-time-equivalent workers in 2023; Massachusetts employed <b>105,348</b>, rank 14 of 50 (derived, SRC-629-03). Individual income taxes were <b>47.8%</b> of Massachusetts FY 2023 state tax collections, rank 5 of 44 (derived, SRC-629-04). State and local revenue was <b>$115.53 billion</b> in Massachusetts in 2022, rank 12 of 51 (derived, SRC-629-05). Public pension systems held <b>$127.85 billion</b> in cash and investments (derived, SRC-629-07). The 2022 Census of Governments counted <b>857</b> government units in Massachusetts (SRC-629-06). State governments employed <b>4,441,091</b> full-time-equivalent workers in 2023; Massachusetts employed <b>105,348</b>, rank 14 of 50 (derived, SRC-629-03). Individual income taxes were <b>47.8%</b> of Massachusetts FY 2023 state tax collections, rank 5 of 44 (derived, SRC-629-04). NASBO rainy-day figures remain pending.",
